build: 2026-06-26 v10.76.35 (FIX black screen — split deep .sheet chain)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notesT: Builds on 10.76.34. THE fix for "Safe Mode oder Black Screen" (build 2068).
  Cause: EchoelStudioView stacked ~24 .sheet/.fullScreenCover modifiers on ONE view —
  a ~30-deep generic type that overflowed the SwiftUI metadata decoder's stack at
  launch (a compile-clean SIGSEGV before anything renders; Safe Mode then caught every
  other launch). The 3 sheets added this session tipped a chain that was already near
  the limit.
  Fix: the presentation modifiers are split into AnyView-bounded groups (screenBase →
  screenSheets1 → screenSheets2 → body), so no single view stacks more than ~8–10
  modifiers and the decoder can't overflow. No feature lost, behaviour identical;
  reviewed for balanced structure + depth. With 10.76.34's self-clearing Safe Mode,
  the trap is fully closed.
  Test: 10.76.35 → cold launch several times → lands straight in the Studio every time
  (no Safe Mode, no black screen). Diagnostics shows the full chain through
  "ui branch: STUDIO — startup task running" → "confirmed healthy".
